<figure class="visual">
  <div class="visual-title">
    <span>01 / Two ways of asking. One evidence trail.</span>
    <span>Illustrative architecture</span>
  </div>
  <div class="evidence-flow">
    <div class="evidence-box">
      <strong>Structured facts</strong>
      <span>dates · values · relationships</span>
    </div>
    <span class="evidence-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      →
    </span>
    <div class="evidence-box">
      <strong>Cypher query</strong>
      <span>precise, bounded checks</span>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-box">
      <strong>Clinical narrative</strong>
      <span>context · negation · uncertainty</span>
    </div>
    <span class="evidence-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
      →
    </span>
    <div class="evidence-box">
      <strong>Evidence retrieval</strong>
      <span>source passages + interpretation</span>
    </div>
    <div class="evidence-merge">Criterion-level assessment → human review</div>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    Both routes should preserve source, time, and uncertainty. A graph
    relationship makes an assertion queryable; it does not make the assertion
    true.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
<figure class="visual">
  <div class="visual-title">
    <span>02 / The same question, three evidence states</span>
    <span>Open a case below</span>
  </div>
  <p style="margin-top:0;color:var(--ink)">
    Fictional inclusion criterion: “At least 28 days since the last dose of
    Therapy X.” Assessment date: November 8, 2026. These are teaching examples,
    not clinical guidance.
  </p>
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary>
      <span class="evidence-state">SUPPORTED</span>Last dose documented on
      September 30
    </summary>
    <p>
      The source explicitly identifies September 30 as the last administration,
      with reconciled treatment history through the assessment date. The
      interval is 39 days, which satisfies this toy criterion. This says nothing
      about the other trial criteria.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary>
      <span class="evidence-state">NOT SATISFIED</span>Confirmed administration
      on November 1
    </summary>
    <p>
      There is a verified dose seven days before assessment. That is enough to
      show the 28-day interval has not elapsed for this toy criterion, even if
      earlier treatment history is incomplete.
    </p>
  </details>
  <details class="evidence-details">
    <summary>
      <span class="evidence-state unknown">UNKNOWN</span>No administration
      appears in the available records
    </summary>
    <p>
      An empty query result cannot establish a last-dose date. Treatment might
      have occurred elsewhere, or the data might not have arrived. Keep the case
      unresolved and identify the missing treatment history instead of silently
      treating it as a pass.
    </p>
  </details>
  <figcaption>
    A criterion can be supported, not satisfied, or unresolved. Trial-level
    eligibility requires the full protocol, applicable exceptions, current
    evidence, and clinical review.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
